    "updated_at": "2020-09-16T21:35:05Z",
    "body": "This seems like a reasonable loosening to me, if it's indeed the route browsers are going down. @rniwa @annevk, any thoughts?\r\n\r\n> I think providing a guarantee within the same callback (stack) makes sense, but I'm not so sure about across async hops. For example:\r\n\r\nProbably the spec way to do that is within the same [task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-task). Since the sentence you mention is already pretty high-level, we could just expand it to\r\n\r\n> Wait until any invocations of this algorithm that had the same method context, <ins>happened during the same [task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-task)</ins>, that started before this one, and whose timeout is equal to or less than this one's, have completed.\r\n\r\n(or some variant of that which makes the now-extra-long sentence a bit more readable.)",
